{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1486754-trinity-in-world-name-for-novas-psions-talents-etc","id":1486754,"title":"[Trinity] In world name for Novas, Psions, Talents, etc?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-17T04:04:59-07:00","id":1486754,"title":"[Trinity] In world name for Novas, Psions, Talents, etc?","content":"Like title - <b>How do you call every (super)humans templates as all the groups (un)humans, in universe?</b><br /> <br /> In <i><b>Adventure! </b></i>era, if I remember correctly, they are called <b>Inspired</b>? Are there other names from different times? How they will be called in Victorian <i><b>Aether</b></i>? How in <i><b>Aegis</b></i> Ancient Greece?<br /> <br /> In <i><b>Aegis,</b></i> I think, they could be <b>Touched ( by Gods )</b>, as <b>Templates </b>are thought of blessed by Gods, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-17-2022, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T06:29:39-07:00","id":1486765,"title":"","content":"Have some scholar describe the lot as Metahumans. Then have &quot;Meta&quot; become the standard slang term. The DCU did that for awhile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T08:25:19-07:00","id":1486769,"title":"","content":"There are 2 levels of \u201cspecial characters\u201d as described in the books:<br /> Inspired: people capable of learning subtle powers that can pass by as overly trained or charlatans. Talents, Mesmerists and Stalwarts are described as Inspired, probably Assassins and Superiors too.<br /> Powered: people capable of learning greater powers. Novas, Psions and Psiads are described as Powered.<br /> <br /> In universe the Way they are called is a bit different.<br /> Inspired would be used during Adventure! Era, but general public is not aware of this idea.<br /> Nova would be used during Nova Era (it covers Psiads and possibly the most overt Assassins and Talents).<br /> Aberrant would be used during Aeon Era to any powered that is not a Psion, including some Psiads. Psiad is more like a urban legend, a Psion that was not dunked, as only Psions can tell the difference between a Quantum user and a Psi user, the result is that anyone that is not a Psion is a Aberrant to the general public.<br /> Aether seams to use Arthernauts for a general description of people that use Aether. But seams like there are those that have powers but not depend on Aether, apparently called Iron Spirit.<br /> Aegis would use the Hero word to describe all of them, because that is what Hero mean, basically superhuman, but it was already stated that they are not going to use it because of obvious reasons (we already have Psion and Scion, that are basically the same word).<br /> <br /> I think it\u2019s important notice that differentiate Quantum from Psi is something new. Even during Nova Era they could identify difference but missed the proper explanation, that would come to be during Aeon era, and mainly so people don\u2019t attack Psions as Aberrants.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see how Aether will deal with the different splats, if it does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-17-2022, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}